      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/47e85d/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2020-04-26T07:28:54.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Or can you declare&nbsp;it after you've seen the Attack result?</p>\n<p>A few other questions:</p>\n<p>Does a basic Defend action defend against all attacks until the player's next turn, or just one attack?</p>\n<p>If an Ability just says, \"until your next turn\" as opposed to \"until the start of your next turn\", does this mean it lasts until the end of your next turn?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:53:45.163Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 2,
      "reads": 4,
      "readers_count": 3,
      "score": 10.8,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 19886,
      "topic_slug": "do-you-have-to-declare-a-defend-reaction-before-the-attack-roll-is-made",
      "display_username": "FastasaTrain",
      "primary_group_name": null,
