    {
      "id": 230353,
      "name": "ErekLich",
      "username": "ErekLich",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/f6c823/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2020-04-26T15:29:42.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Chapter 2 describes a Reaction as happening \"in response to a certain trigger\" and each Reaction describes the conditions under which it is usable.&nbsp; So the real question is, does the \"when you are attacked\" style trigger come before or after the roll?&nbsp; Given that there are also triggers which say \"when damaged\" a super-strict reading would be that \"when attacked\" is when the attack is declared.&nbsp; That said, my group (who never stopped to actually consider the question) has basically been doing it after the roll, and it certainly doesn't break the game!&nbsp; So I'd say ask your GM.</p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:05:19.664Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 1,
      "reads": 4,
      "readers_count": 3,
      "score": 0.8,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 19886,
      "topic_slug": "do-you-have-to-declare-a-defend-reaction-before-the-attack-roll-is-made",
      "display_username": "ErekLich",
      "primary_group_name": null,
