      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Chapter 2 describes a Reaction as happening \"in response to a certain trigger\" and each Reaction describes the conditions under which it is usable.&nbsp; So the real question is, does the \"when you are attacked\" style trigger come before or after the roll?&nbsp; Given that there are also triggers which say \"when damaged\" a super-strict reading would be that \"when attacked\" is when the attack is declared.&nbsp; That said, my group (who never stopped to actually consider the question) has basically been doing it after the roll, and it certainly doesn't break the game!&nbsp; So I'd say ask your GM.</p>",
