    {
      "id": 230359,
      "name": "Sonvar",
      "username": "Powerhound_2000",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
      "created_at": "2020-04-27T11:53:25.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"FastasaTrain\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/47e85d/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> FastasaTrain:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>catDreaming wrote:</b><br>\n<blockquote>A Defend action lasts until it is used to block damage, or the start of it's creator's turn. Whichever comes first.\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n<p>Am I right in assuming that if the hero gets attacked multiple times that they can choose any one of those attacks to Defend <br><br>\nagainst? As opposed to being restricted to defending against the first attack against them.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>There is no choice.   From the core rulebook in chapter 2 it calls out it used up the next time you take damage and if you aren’t attacked by your next turn the effect expires.  Some abilities will allow you to maintain a defend against all attacks on you until your next turn but the explicitly call it out.   If an ability doesn’t state that and just has a defend effect on it then it works only against the next attack on you until your next turn.    There is an option when using a Defend action to protect another hero instead but it again gets used up either by the next attack on that hero or until your next turn.</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
