      "raw": "[quote=\"FastasaTrain\"]\n\n<div class=\"bb-quote\"><b>catDreaming wrote:</b><br />\n<blockquote class=\"bb-quote-body\">A Defend action lasts until it is used to block damage, or the start of it's creator's turn. Whichever comes first.\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n\nAm I right in assuming that if the hero gets attacked multiple times that they can choose any one of those attacks to Defend <br />\nagainst? As opposed to being restricted to defending against the first attack against them.\n\n[/quote]\n\nThere is no choice.   From the core rulebook in chapter 2 it calls out it used up the next time you take damage and if you aren’t attacked by your next turn the effect expires.  Some abilities will allow you to maintain a defend against all attacks on you until your next turn but the explicitly call it out.   If an ability doesn’t state that and just has a defend effect on it then it works only against the next attack on you until your next turn.    There is an option when using a Defend action to protect another hero instead but it again gets used up either by the next attack on that hero or until your next turn.",
